    "source": "Bluebeam area markup drawn by Aryan (U0BCUEBAAFQ) and posted to #fortel on 2026-08-26, Slack ts 1787736005.186649, Google Drive id 1UMauqocw-rCw5_gA_RhUcWD0GDbmqu5Q. The marked PDF differs from the unmarked sheet by exactly two vector paths: this polygon and its label box reading 'Unclassified area - 9,810.24 m2'. The marked PDF itself is kept OUT of drawings/ (at ~/fortel-ground-truth/) because the robustness corpus scans that tree and would otherwise measure the markup as if it were a client drawing; nothing here depends on the PDF, the vertices below are the artefact.",
    "corroboration": "Independent shoelace over the extracted vertices gives 9810.12 m2, 0.001% from the markup's own label, which also confirms the sheet's 1:500 / k=0.176389 is read correctly. 94.6% of the sheet's red-tint (254,0,0) ink falls inside this polygon, so it is the right region and not an area coincidence. Inderjit quoted 9,857 m2 for the same yard on the 5 Aug call.",
    "note": "The yard is drawn as RED DIAGONAL HATCHING, not a solid fill: 1 px strokes, median inter-stroke gap 26 px (2.29 m at 1:500), inking only 2.8% of the area they enclose. This is the reference case for hatch-aware detection."
  },
